{
  "esm": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "latlon3d_advection_vertical_ppm_mono",
    "description": "MMS driver: MONOTONE conservative flux-form vertical advection on the 3-D latlon3d grid, u_t = -D(u, lev) + src, discretized by grids/latlon3d/rules/ppm_D_lev_mono_noflux_bc (full Colella-Woodward 1984 PPM: eq (1.6) edge on eq (1.8) monotonized slopes plus the eq (1.10) parabola limiter; non-uniform finite-volume flux divergence (w u)_z with genuine no-flux top/surface, rank-3). The PRODUCTION-grade counterpart of latlon3d_advection_vertical_ppm (same operator, unlimited reconstruction): identical manufactured solution, identical mesh, identical forcing -- the ONLY difference is the imported rule, so the two convergence goldens isolate exactly what the monotonicity limiter costs in order (4.0 -> ~2.5 L2 / ~2.0 Linf) and, read alongside the rule's boundedness claim, what it buys. FLUX-FORM (the velocity w_edge enters inside the operator, so the consumer writes u_t=-D(u,lev)+src, NOT -w*D). PASSIVE lon (NLON=8) and lat (NLAT=5). Manufactured STEADY solution u*(z)=cos(pi z) (as cell averages) with vertical velocity w(z)=sin(pi z) that VANISHES at the surface and model top (natural no-flux, exact mass conservation) and matching steady forcing src = cell-average of (w u*)_z; u_t=0 continuously, so the discrete drift is pure flux-divergence truncation. NOTE the limiter's fingerprint: cos(pi z) has its extrema exactly AT the two walls (cos'(0)=cos'(pi)=0), which is where eq (1.8)/(1.10) clip hardest, so Linf lags L2. VERTICAL MESH: the consumer supplies pe (quadratic stretch, shape [lev_nodes]); the grid derives dz via lev_thickness; w_edge=sin(pi pe) is the interface velocity. HYGIENE: pe over kn, w_edge over kw, dz via gk -- all distinct from the operator's k. ic/references spell the cell-average of cos(pi z) inline from the stretch formula and the NLEV name (build-time scope caveat).",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": [
      "esd:problem",
      "grid:latlon3d",
      "equation:advection",
      "mms"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Colella, P., & Woodward, P. R. (1984). The Piecewise Parabolic Method (PPM) for gas-dynamical simulations. Journal of Computational Physics, 54(1), 174-201.",
        "doi": "10.1016/0021-9991(84)90143-8"
      },
      {
        "citation": "Colella, P., & Sekora, M. D. (2008). A limiter for PPM that preserves accuracy at smooth extrema. Journal of Computational Physics, 227(15), 7069-7076.",
        "doi": "10.1016/j.jcp.2008.03.034"
      },
      {
        "citation": "Lin, S.-J., & Rood, R. B. (1996). Multidimensional flux-form semi-Lagrangian transport schemes. Monthly Weather Review, 124(9), 2046-2070.",
        "doi": "10.1175/1520-0493(1996)124<2046:MFFSLT>2.0.CO;2"
      },
      {
        "citation": "Roache, P. J. (2002). Code verification by the method of manufactured solutions. J. Fluids Eng. 124(1), 4-10.",
        "doi": "10.1115/1.1436090"
      }
    ]
  },
  "models": {
    "VerticalAdvectionPPMMono3d": {
      "expression_template_imports": [
        {
          "ref": "../grids/latlon3d/rules/ppm_D_lev_mono_noflux_bc.esm",
          "bindings": {
            "NLON": 8,
            "NLAT": 5
          }
        }
      ],
      "variables": {
        "u": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "lon",
            "lat",
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Advected tracer over lon x lat x lev (horizontally uniform here); treated as cell averages for the finite-volume flux-form scheme."
        },
        "pe": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "lev_nodes"
          ],
          "description": "Level-edge coordinates of the quadratic-stretch vertical mesh, pe[kn]=0.6((kn-1)/NLEV)+0.4((kn-1)/NLEV)^2 over node kn=1..NLEV+1 (pe[1]=0, pe[NLEV+1]=1). HYGIENE: aggregates over the node index `kn` (not k), so inlined pe[k]/dz[k]/w_edge[k] reads do not capture the operator's k."
        },
        "dz": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Cell thicknesses dz[k]=pe[k+1]-pe[k] via the grid's lev_thickness template: the grid's dz free name read by grids/latlon3d/rules/ppm_D_lev_noflux_bc. lev_thickness uses the grid-hygienic index gk, distinct from the operator's k."
        },
        "w_edge": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1/s",
          "shape": [
            "lev_nodes"
          ],
          "description": "Vertical velocity at cell interfaces, w_edge[kw]=sin(pi pe[kw]): the grid's w_edge free name read by the flux-form operator. VANISHES at the surface (pe[1]=0 -> sin 0 = 0) and model top (pe[NLEV+1]=1 -> sin pi = 0), so the wall fluxes are identically zero and the scheme is exactly mass-conserving. aggregates over `kw` (distinct from k)."
        },
        "src": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1/s",
          "shape": [
            "lon",
            "lat",
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Steady forcing = analytic cell-average of the flux divergence (w u*)_z with w=sin(pi z), u*=cos(pi z): w u* = 0.5 sin(2 pi z), so (w u*)_z cell-average = (0.5 sin(2 pi pe[k+1]) - 0.5 sin(2 pi pe[k]))/dz[k]. Reads pe and dz at runtime; holds u*=cos(pi z) steady so the discrete drift is pure flux-divergence truncation."
        }
      },
