      "tests": [
        {
          "id": "mms_steady_vertical_ppm_mono_3d",
          "description": "Manufactured steady u*(z)=cos(pi z) (cell averages) transported by w(z)=sin(pi z) in flux form, u_t = -(w u)_lev + src with src the analytic cell-average flux divergence, so u_t=0 continuously; the discrete field drifts only by flux-divergence truncation. t=0 pins the cell-average ic wiring; t=0.1 bounds the drift (measured ~2.5 order in L2 / ~2.0 in Linf on the stretched mesh -- the CW84 eq (1.8)+(1.10) limiters clip the smooth extrema of cos(pi z), which sit AT the two walls, so the order falls from the unlimited chain's clean 4.0; that is the deliberate cost of boundedness). Because w vanishes at both walls the scheme is still exactly mass-conserving (limiting changes edge VALUES, not the single-valued-ness of each face flux; verified machine-zero, not asserted here since the source term makes the forced total non-invariant). This smooth MMS measures ORDER, not the property the monotone variant exists for: boundedness on SHARP gradients (where the unlimited sibling drives the tracer negative and this one does not) is a separate, structural claim carried by the rule. Per-resolution errors in the convergence golden.",
